<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ley Paccionada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ley Paccionada de Navarra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ley Paccionada is the Spanish law of 16 August 1841 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre</a>'s status as a separate realm after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-carlist-war">First Carlist War</a>. Negotiated between Navarre's representatives and the government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, it made Navarre a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> while preserving its own provincial council and a special fiscal and administrative regime. It remains the legal foundation of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foral-community-of-navarre">Foral Community of Navarre</a>.</p></div>
